  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                 ; continued
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=900
                                                               ; THE SCHEDULE BUFFER REVERSED  round key by round key
                                                               ; so that the SAME conveyor feeds a decryption;
;
                                                               ; FIPS 197 section 5 point 3 consumes the round keys
                                                               ; last to first; the buffer holds them first to last
                                                               ; because that is the order they are made in and
                                                               ; block/rkappend208 can only append; A second conveyor
                                                               ; reading from the far end cannot be written at all:
                                                               ; the far end MOVES as the buffer empties  so its
                                                               ; address would be a computed offset  which is the one
                                                               ; thing the conveyor rule exists to forbid; So the
                                                               ; buffer is turned round once  here  and
                                                               ; block/rkconsume208 then runs unchanged;
;
                                                               ; ONE CONSUMER IN THE LIBRARY  which is what this is
                                                               ; for; a decryption is then the same text as an
                                                               ; encryption apart from the round body: both take
                                                               ; sixteen bytes off the front and slide; A mirrored
                                                               ; consumer would have been the same number of lines and
                                                               ; would have left two routines to keep right;
;
                                                               ; IT IS CHEAP AND IT IS ONCE; six swaps of sixteen
                                                               ; bytes is two hundred and eighty eight moves  against
                                                               ; a decryption whose conveyor costs that much EVERY
                                                               ; round  thirteen times over; The middle group does not
                                                               ; move and the arithmetic says so rather than a special
                                                               ; case: with thirteen groups there are six pairs and
                                                               ; one left over;
;
                                                               ; THE BYTES INSIDE A ROUND KEY DO NOT TURN  only the
                                                               ; groups do; A reversal carried all the way down to the
                                                               ; byte would hand each round a key with its bytes
                                                               ; backwards  and produce sixteen plausible bytes at the
                                                               ; end; No contract here can see that; only a vector can
                                                               ; which is why the published ones go both ways;
;
                                                               ; THE SCRATCH IS THE BLOCK'S OWN  sixteen cells
                                                               ; immediately above the buffer  claimed clear at both
                                                               ; ends;
;
                                                               ; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset
                                                               ; resolves them;
;
                                                               ; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x000:0x0cf  the schedule buffer{208}  turned round in place
;   @0x0d0:0x0df  scratch{16}  one round key in transit
;
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=900
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 1108:1123

