                                                               ; INV SHIFT ROWS AND INV SUB BYTES over the state at
                                                               ; @0x052:0x061  which between them are the AES inverse
                                                               ; cipher's final round  and the first two thirds of
                                                               ; every other one;
;
                                                               ; FIPS 197 section 5 point 3; This is
                                                               ; block/aesroundlast's mirror and the two differ in
                                                               ; exactly two ways: the rows turn RIGHT rather than
                                                               ; left  and the steps come in the other order; The
                                                               ; forward round substitutes and then shifts; the
                                                               ; inverse shifts and then substitutes; That is not a
                                                               ; style choice  it is what makes the two functions
                                                               ; inverses;
;
                                                               ; THE SUBSTITUTION IS THE SAME SIXTEEN WALKS  character
                                                               ; for character  as block/aesroundlast's; There is no
                                                               ; InvSubBytes code anywhere in this file: the walk
                                                               ; reads whatever table is resident at @0x075  and a
                                                               ; caller that has swapped the forward S box for the
                                                               ; inverse one gets InvSubBytes from the identical
                                                               ; instructions; That is the whole reason the table is a
                                                               ; swap rather than a second table at a second address;
;
                                                               ; WHICH MEANS A DEFECT IN A WALK CANNOT BE PRESENT IN
                                                               ; ONE DIRECTION AND ABSENT FROM THE OTHER  and the
                                                               ; forward vectors already pin the walk;
;
                                                               ; THE TABLE SURVIVES; block/walk256 copies each datum
                                                               ; it reads and puts it back  so the inverse table is
                                                               ; still readable after a round and a caller lays it
                                                               ; once;
;
                                                               ; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset
                                                               ; resolves them;
;
                                                               ; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x052:0x061  state{16}  read and written in place
;   @0x072:0x374  group 0 of the walk and the table above it  READ ONLY
;
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=0

                                                               ; InvShiftRows  pasted where the state already is; it
                                                               ; comes FIRST here  which is the order the inverse
                                                               ; cipher has and the forward one does not
